      "title": "docs(skills): expand glab-stack guidance for non-interactive reorder and infer",
      "description": "## Description\n\nFollow-up to https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/merge_requests/4267, which made `glab stack reorder` and `glab stack infer` usable without a TTY. That MR updated the bundled `glab-stack` skill, but agents following the skill could still get stuck or leave GitLab out of sync. This MR fills those gaps:\n\n- **`infer` needs `--name` when no stack is active.** Without it, `infer --all` fails with \"no stack found and no TTY available\". Rule 6 now says so, and there's a new quick-reference row.\n- **`reorder` only rebases locally.** Rule 5 now says to run `glab stack sync` afterwards to force-push.\n- **Reorder conflict recovery.** A new section covers `git rebase --continue` followed by `glab stack reorder --continue` or `--abort`. Both commands are also in the quick reference.\n- **Branch-list rules for `reorder`.** List every branch exactly once, the first branch sits on the base branch, and commit or stash tracked changes first.\n- **Wording.** `reorder` and `infer` without the new arguments now \"hang or fail without a TTY\", and the skill description mentions inferring a stack from commits.\n\n## Related Issues\n\nRelated to #8658\n\n## How has this been tested?\n\nDocs-only change to `SKILL.md`. The `validate-skills` and markdownlint hooks pass, as do the `internal/commands/skills` tests.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
